#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_jacobi_sn

#% text
# `inverse_jacobi_sn(v, m)` gives the `u` with `jacobi_sn(u, m) = v`, the principal value `elliptic_f(asin(v), m)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 22.15.12; for real `-1 <= v <= 1` and `m < 1` the value is real.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_sn(0.5, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.5356227328054033

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_sn(1.0, 0.5) - elliptic_k(0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_sn(-0.3, 0.9)
#% output
#= -0.3090180530675288

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `jacobi_sn` undoes it:

#% cell
jacobi_sn(inverse_jacobi_sn(0.4, 0.3), 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.4

#% text
# The relation to `elliptic_f`:

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_sn(0.4, 0.3) - elliptic_f(asin(0.4), 0.3)
#% output
#= -5.551115123125783e-17

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `jacobi_sn`, `elliptic_f`, `inverse_jacobi_cn`, `inverse_jacobi_dn`
